   "id": 542303,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Find the complement of the Graph <i>H</i>.\n<figure>\n<img src=\"exercises/media/088188e9fe6bfa87.png\" alt=\"Graph H has five vertices. The vertices are A, B, C, D, and E. The edges connect A E, A D, A B, A C, E D, D C, and C B.\">\n</figure>",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>One way to find the complement of a graph is to draw the complete graph with the same number of vertices and remove all the edges that were in the original graph.</p>\n<p>Vertex <i>A</i> has a degree of 0.</p>\n<p>The other vertices will be connected in a line, <i>C</i> to <i>E</i> to <i>B</i> to <i>D</i>. Each will have a degree of 2.</p>\n<p>The edges are <i>BD, CE, EB</i>.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<br>\n<img src=\"https://exercises.openstax.org/rails/active_storage/blobs/proxy/eyJfcmFpbHMiOnsibWVzc2FnZSI6IkJBaHBBcEVOIiwiZXhwIjpudWxsLCJwdXIiOiJibG9iX2lkIn19--2f6a7748bad153abee272459070822f472a08539/CS_Figure_12_03_079.png\" alt=\"The complement of graph H is displayed. The vertices are A, B, C, D, and E. The edges connect B E, B D, and E C.\">\n"
    }
